From: notrealOS <53965041+notrealdotmp4@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: awb: Keep all gains at least 1.0

With a red gain below 1 (warm light), sensor-clipped highlights come out
cyan instead of white because the debayer clamps after the gains.
---
--- a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/awb.cpp	2026-10-09 23:08:55.162414814 +0200
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/awb.cpp	2026-10-09 23:08:55.228116080 +0200
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 
 #include "awb.h"
 
+#include <algorithm>
 #include <numeric>
 #include <stdint.h>
 
@@ -88,6 +89,17 @@
 	context.activeState.awb.temperatureK = estimateCCT(rgbGains);
 	metadata.set(controls::ColourTemperature, context.activeState.awb.temperatureK);
 
+	/*
+	 * Keep every gain at 1.0 or above. The debayer clamps each channel to the
+	 * sensor range right after the gains, so with a gain below 1.0 a channel
+	 * that clipped in the sensor ends up below full scale while the others
+	 * saturate: blown-out highlights turn cyan under warm light (red gain < 1)
+	 * instead of white. Real ISPs normalise the smallest gain to 1.0 for this.
+	 */
+	const float minGain = std::min({ gains.r(), gains.g(), gains.b() });
+	if (minGain < 1.0f)
+		gains /= minGain;
+
 	LOG(IPASoftAwb, Debug)
 		<< "gain R/B: " << gains << "; temperature: "
 		<< context.activeState.awb.temperatureK;
